# =============================================================================
#  nasa-bearing-anomaly
#
#  Every rule below carries the reason it exists. A rule whose reason is gone
#  should be deleted, not left behind "just in case".
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Data — raw
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The NASA IMS vibration archive is ~6.2 GB. Never committed.
# data/README.md carries the download link, the expected folder layout, and the
# Set 3 file-count discrepancy a cloner has to know about.
#
# The trailing /* matters: with `data/raw/` git would not descend into the
# directory at all, so the .gitkeep negation below could never match and a clone
# would arrive with no data/raw/ for the loader to write into.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Data — reference PDFs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Papers kept beside the code while working. One of them is published by
# Elsevier and may not be redistributed; putting it in a public repository is a
# copyright problem that cannot be undone once it is in git history. The papers
# are cited in data/README.md — they are not shipped.
data/docs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Data — processed
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three per-file summary tables ARE committed, deliberately: the raw input is
# a 6.2 GB download, so without them nobody can run notebooks 02-04 from a clone.
#
# The negation names them individually rather than *.csv. The enriched feature
# tables (test{N}_features.csv) are derived from these three in seconds and are
# several times larger, so committing them would cost tens of megabytes and buy
# nothing. Anything else dropped here — pickles, parquet, checkpoints — is scratch.
data/processed/*
!data/processed/test1_raw.csv
!data/processed/test2_raw.csv
!data/processed/test3_raw.csv

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Results — mostly committed on purpose
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# results/figures/ is the evidence behind the claims in the README, not scratch,
# so it is committed. Same for the summary tables in results/reports/. The
# *.pt / *.pkl / *.joblib rules below catch model checkpoints if any land here.
#
# The per-test scored frames are the exception. detection writes back the entire
# feature table it was given -- around 200 columns of rolling and difference
# features -- with three result columns appended, so each file is 99% a copy of
# its own input and they total tens of megabytes. They regenerate in seconds from
# the committed tables, and they exist only to hand data from notebook 03 to
# notebook 04, which recreates them when they are absent. The one-row-per-test
# summary beside them is the actual artifact and stays committed.
results/reports/*_results.csv

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Working notes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Planning documents, status files, scratch TODOs. Working material, not
# portfolio content, and it dates far faster than the code does.
/plan/

# The decision log is working material too: it records what was chosen, what was
# rejected and why, in the terms the work was argued in. Naming it here is safe --
# unlike the agent-rules files, the name discloses nothing about the tooling, and
# a rule at repo root is what stops an untracked file at repo root being added by
# a stray `git add .`.
/DECISIONS.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Rendered site
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Quarto site is rendered locally and published to the gh-pages branch.
# main holds source only — a committed site is what turns a 3 MB repo into 26 MB.
/_site/
/.quarto/
/_freeze/

# Quarto writes a .quarto_ipynb beside each notebook it renders, as the
# intermediate it hands to pandoc. `quarto render` appends this rule itself if it
# is absent; it is written here explicitly so the pattern sits with the other
# build artefacts and carries its reason, rather than being appended unexplained
# after the secrets section.
**/*.quarto_ipynb

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Python
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.egg

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Environments
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listed for completeness only. This project uses conda; environment.yml and
# pyproject.toml between them describe the environment, and neither is ignored.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Test and lint caches
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Jupyter
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebook OUTPUTS are stripped from commits by the nbstripout git clean filter,
# configured in .gitattributes — not by a rule here, and not by a pre-commit
# hook. The filter rewrites only the blob git stores, so the outputs stay on disk
# where Quarto renders the site from them. A stripping pre-commit hook would
# erase them on disk instead; do not add one. See README.md.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Model checkpoints
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PyTorch autoencoder weights and pickled sklearn estimators. Regenerated by
# re-running the pipeline, and a pickle is not reviewable in a diff.
*.pt
*.pth
*.pkl
*.joblib

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Editors and IDEs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  OS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Secrets
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No secret is needed to run this project — the dataset is a public download.
# These rules are a floor, not a description of what exists.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
